Reason: port: an exact state load waits up to kStateLoadWaitFrames for the game's threads (and a disc read) to stand as they did when the state was saved, instead of falling back at once to the portable load, which restarts the level's actors and replays its intro. Only those passing conditions wait; another build or game still loads the portable way at once.
A portable load finishes once the state's area is reached, whatever episode the game picked for it (Delfino Plaza follows the story); waiting for the saved episode there held every state request off for 20 seconds and ended in "Could not load the state".
While a load is under way it tells platform/savestate (port_savestate_set_loading), so a request meanwhile says the state is still loading instead of "not in a level".
